**Standard deviation of the null‑hypothesis test (standard error)**  

\[
SE = \frac{s}{\sqrt{n}}
    = \frac{1.4}{\sqrt{40}}
    \approx \frac{1.4}{6.3249}
    \approx 0.221
\]

So the standard deviation of the sampling distribution of the mean under the null hypothesis is **≈ 0.22**.
